  "narrative": "No assessments are due. The core evidence remains feature_002=1, feature_010=1, and feature_037=1; I am not reopening those claims. The next most informative questions are portability and context specificity of newly found residual signals. feature_027=1 shows a large negative association with outcome_001 in the core-flag-free population, and feature_063=1 shows a smaller negative association there. I registered direct negative-direction tests of both features within each core-flag-positive stratum (feature_002=1, feature_010=1, feature_037=1). If the associations remain in these strata, they are more likely residual predictors than artifacts of the core-flag-free conditioning set; if they vanish or reverse, they are context-dependent relative to the core flags. Full-population H113/H114 should also be prioritized because they test whether the overall association is preserved or diluted after accounting for core-flag-positive participants.\n\nFor feature_003, the residual negative signal is near threshold overall but was strong in high feature_018 and high feature_036 core-free contexts, though validation failed to clear threshold for the high feature_018 context. I registered a joint high-context test (feature_018>=0.5 and feature_036>=0.5) to see whether the feature_003 association concentrates in a shared high-assay-signature state rather than in a single arbitrary half split. This is still dataset-specific and not a biological pathway claim.\n\nFinally, I completed the rare-binary residual screen for five untested features within the core-flag-free population: feature_017, feature_043, feature_022, feature_028, and feature_064. The nominal positive direction is used because these are opaque binaries with no assigned role; large opposite effects would be followed by reversed claims if threshold-relevant. If all are null or subthreshold, the residual rare-binary screen can be closed as mostly negative, leaving feature_027, feature_063, and feature_